Filters: p adjusts direct receive bandwidth; l adjusts Low Cut; u adjusts Upper Cut where supported. Full stop increases; comma decreases. Starts at the current setting and stops at each end. q keeps the setting and returns to Filters; q again returns to the top level. h gives help. In high/low-cut configuration, p directs you to l or u. Changing one edge keeps the other edge unchanged. Fixed widths remain unchanged. Unsupported controls or modes say Not supported. A symbolic Yaesu default is reported without guessing its width; select a numeric width on the radio before adjusting. QMX uses enabled CW passbands or SSB receive width; menu changes are saved by the radio and may automatically adjust its CW centre/offset/sidetone according to radio settings.

Noise Blanker: f then b toggles the current state and reports On or Off. Inside the control, b toggles again. Full stop increases level; comma decreases it. When off, navigation reports Off and leaves the level unchanged. q returns to Filters; q again returns to the top level. h gives help. Levels use the radio scale, or percent where defined. Unknown status prevents a toggle. FTX-1 remembers the last on level observed by YAC, separately for Main/Sub; when none is known, On uses level 1. TS-590SG remembers the last observed NB1/NB2 selection; when none is known, On selects NB1. Unsupported radios or modes report Not supported.

Noise Reduction: f then r toggles the current state; r inside toggles again. Full stop increases the setting; comma decreases it; endpoints do not loop. While Off, navigation leaves the setting unchanged and reports Off. q returns to Filters; q again returns to the top level. h gives help. FTDX10/FT-710 levels are 1-15; FTX-1 levels 1-10, remembered separately per Main/Sub, with level 1 used if no previous on level is known. Icom levels are reported as percentages. Kenwood retains the last observed NR1/NR2 type; if unknown, On selects NR1. TS-590SG NR1 levels are 1-10. TS-480 NR1 offers Auto then 1-9; comma from 1 selects Auto. NR2 following time is 2-20 milliseconds. Nav follows the radio current NR type; it does not select the other type. Choose a different type on the radio if needed. Unsupported radios or modes report Not supported; unknown state prevents a toggle.

In Kenwood FM mode, switching On selects NR1.

Notch: f then a toggles Auto Notch; a inside toggles again. TS-480 uses Beat Cancel instead, retaining the last observed BC1/BC2 type, defaulting to BC1. f then n toggles Manual Notch; n inside toggles again. Full stop/comma raise/lower its frequency or position while On, stopping at endpoints. w inside Manual Notch cycles width. While Off, movement and w keep settings unchanged. q returns to Filters; q again returns to the top level; h gives help. Yaesu reports 10-3200 hertz; Icom reports position 0-255; TS-590SG reports position 0-127. Width choices follow manufacturer names. Where Auto/Manual are mutually exclusive, switching one On switches the other Off. TS-590SG restores the last manual width observed by YAC; if none is known, first On uses and announces Normal. Select BC1/BC2 on the TS-480 radio if a different type is needed. Unsupported functions/modes report Not supported; unknown status prevents toggling. QMX has no documented notch control.

Contour: f c toggles On/Off. Navigation adjusts current frequency (10-3200 hertz). Inside Contour, l selects Contour level (-40 to +20, spoken as Dip/Neutral/Peak); w selects Contour width (1-11); c returns to frequency. When already on frequency, c toggles On/Off. Full stop increases and comma decreases the selected setting, stopping at endpoints. Off leaves settings unchanged. q returns to Filters, where l means Low Cut; q again returns to top level. Current settings are preserved on switching. FT-DX10, FT-710 and FTX-1 only; FTX-1 frequency/state follow selected Main/Sub, level/width are shared menu settings. APF is separate and is not altered.

Filter Verify: f v lists switchable filters currently On for the current mode/receiver, using live readback. v inside any filter adjustment gives the same report without leaving the control. Off and unsupported filters are omitted; unreadable states are announced as unknown. If every applicable state is known and Off, says No switchable filters On. Bandwidth/low/upper cuts have no switchable On/Off state and are not included. FTX-1 reports Main or Sub. Verify changes no settings.

Repeated v review: first v gives the filters-On summary. Further consecutive v presses show one applicable filter at a time, including Off or unknown, then return to the summary. Each status is read live. Any other command restarts the next v at the summary; a receive-mode or receiver change also restarts review. q leaves Filters when at the submenu; inside an adjustment, q first returns to Filters. Main v is unchanged.
